 status and quality of life.\",3\r\n9664,INTESTINE,\"The intestine is a crucial component of the digestive system, playing a significant role in the absorption of nutrients, which is essential for overall nutrition. Additionally, the intestine is involved in gluconeogenesis, contributing to the production of glucose in the body. However, it is important to note that the intestine can also be a site of inflammation and damage in individuals with celiac disease, where gluten triggers adverse reactions. Thus, the health of the intestine is vital not only for nutrient absorption and glucose production but also for preventing inflammatory conditions related to dietary components.\",2\r\n12517,ACIDOSIS D-LÁCTICA,\"Acidosis D-láctica is a significant complication in patients with SIC, resulting from the fermentation of undigested carbohydrates by Lactobacillus.\",1\r\n12515,DAPTOMICINA,Daptomicina is an antibiotic that is effective against biofilms formed on central venous catheters and is used in the treatment of infections related to these catheters.,1\r\n12514,EHAFI,\"EHAFI refers to a condition that requires specific prophylactic measures to be applied in patients, particularly in the context of nutritional support and lipid administration.\",1\r\n12519,FISTULA ARTERIOVENOSA,\"An arteriovenous fistula may be beneficial for some patients for the administration of NPD, providing an alternative access route.\",1\r\n12479,INTENSIVE NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT,Intensive nutritional support is a treatment approach for patients with intestinal failure to maintain nutritional status and prevent malnutrition.,1\r\n12487,TRÁNSITO INTESTINAL,Tránsito intestinal is a diagnostic procedure involving the use of contrast to assess the length of the remaining intestine and its functionality.,1\r\n7059,ESTUDIO STEPS,The STEPS study investigated the effects of teduglutide on patients with short bowel syndrome and their nutritional needs.,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source